      "title": "PNB: Stressed Loan Auctions And Results Will Guide Balanced Outlook",
      "body": "The analyst price target for Punjab National Bank has been adjusted slightly higher from ₹130.56 to ₹131.76, with analysts citing updated assumptions on fair value, discount rate, revenue growth, profit margin and future P/E as the basis for the change. What's in the News CFM ARC has emerged as the anchor bidder to take over ₹5,140 million of Gammon India’s debt from Punjab National Bank through a Swiss auction process, with an initial all cash offer of ₹1,400 million that implies about a 73% haircut on PNB’s exposure.",
