    {
      "id": "12253e18-e0d5-423d-ba71-8b5396d99759",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-02-23T00:00:00.000Z",
      "title": "CFM ARC Reportedly Leads Race for Gammon India's INR 5,140 Million Debt",
      "body": "CFM ARC (CFM Asset Reconstruction Private Limited) has emerged as the anchor bidder to takeover the INR 5,140 million debt of engineering, procurement and construction (EPC) company Gammon India Ltd. from state-owned Punjab National Bank (NSEI:PNB). Documents accessed by ET show that PNB has called for a challenging bid to the INR 1,400 million all cash offer it received from CFM ARC for its INR 5,140 million loans in the EPC company. \"The bank has initiated a Swiss auction to find a better price on an all cash basis. Bidding is likely via an electronic auction next week. From CFM's perspective, it will help the company to consolidate Gammon's debt,\" said a person aware of the details. CFM's offer at INR 1,400 million means about a 73% haircut for PNB on the company's total exposure of INR",
      "keyDevTypeId": "65",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
